  "body": "Found while checking #2610 (closed: not a bug). The `G10 L20 P<n> X[#5420-#190]` line in `tormach.cps` and `linuxcnc.cps` writes the target WCS as the ACTIVE work offset plus the probed deviation; the old target origin, tool length and G92 cancel out (decisions #173, #362; `fanuc.cps` does the same with `G10 L2`).\n\nNo test pins this: the probe tests assert only the text of the `G10 L20` line, and the in-repo controller model is Fanuc-only. A later change could break the arithmetic without a red test.\n\nDone means: a test (post crate) evaluates the posted probe program for an active WCS and a different target WCS with different origins, and asserts the target's new origin = active origin + deviation, for both posts.\n\nPart of #2610's follow-up.\n",
